From e765bc0d4b9f68fc17c940ed4e9a0f2bb3552f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:17:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rednsd: vendor nghttp2 1.71.0 (MIT) for DNS-over-HTTPS (102.8
 line)

nghttp2, the HTTP/2 C library, unmodified upstream sources of release 1.71.0 under rednsd/nghttp2
(lib/ and its headers, COPYING), with README.reaper saying what is used and why. Only rednsd
compiles it in (the next commit); no shared object, nothing else links it. 1.64.0 or newer is
required for the stream-reset and CONTINUATION limits; the outbound queue limit is new in 1.71.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
