+nghttp2 in rednsd (vendored 2026-11-10)
+=======================================
+
+What     nghttp2, the HTTP/2 C library - https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2 (MIT, see COPYING).
+         Only rednsd uses it, for its DNS-over-HTTPS listener; rednsd/Makefile compiles these
+         sources straight into the rednsd binary. No shared object, nothing else links it.
+
+Version  1.71.0 (upstream release of 2026-11-02; the newest stable release on 2026-11-10).
+         1.64.0 or newer is required: rednsd sets the stream-reset rate limit and the
+         CONTINUATION limit through nghttp2_option. It also uses
+         nghttp2_option_set_max_outbound_queue_size(), which is new in 1.71.0.
+
+Source   nghttp2-1.71.0.tar.xz from https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/releases/tag/v1.71.0
+         sha256 c0f55121d88650e4b9227aec28cebaf664d2417ca60fe70be0f8d38829f52116
+
+Checked  - the tarball's sha256 equals the one in the release's own checksums.txt and the
+           digest GitHub reports for the release asset;
+         - every file here is byte-identical to the file of the same path in that tarball.
+Not      the tarball's OpenPGP signature (nghttp2-1.71.0.tar.xz.asc, RSA key
+checked  516B622918D15C478AB1EA3A5339A2BE82E07DEC, made 2026-11-02): the signer's public key
+         was not fetched, so the signature was not verified. The checksum and the signature
+         file come from the same release page - they show the download is intact, not who
+         made it.
+
+Taken    55 files, 1,064,158 bytes:
+           lib/*.c (26) and lib/*.h (26)                        the library
+           lib/includes/nghttp2/nghttp2.h                       its public header
+           lib/includes/nghttp2/nghttp2ver.h                    the version header, as the
+               release tarball ships it (upstream generates it from nghttp2ver.h.in when it
+               makes the release: NGHTTP2_VERSION "1.71.0", NGHTTP2_VERSION_NUM 0x014700)
+           COPYING                                              the licence
+Left     everything else: the build systems (configure, automake, cmake, lib/Makefile*,
+out      lib/CMakeLists.txt, lib/*.in), the applications and their C++ (src/), third-party/,
+         tests/, fuzz/, doc/, examples/, integration-tests/, the Python and Go helpers.
+
+Changes  none. No upstream file is modified. What configure would have put into config.h is
+         given as -D flags in rednsd/Makefile, with the reason for each.
+
+Updating Take the newest stable release, check the tarball as above, replace the files of
+         the same paths (add or drop names in the Makefile's NGH2_OBJS if lib/*.c changed),
+         update this file, and run build-scripts/tests/test_rednsd.py: it builds rednsd with
+         these sources and drives the DoH listener, once more under ASan/UBSan.
+         To compare this directory with a tarball:
+           tar -xJf nghttp2-X.Y.Z.tar.xz && diff -r nghttp2-X.Y.Z/lib <here>/lib | grep -v '^Only in nghttp2-'
